We need to address runtime errors that caused canvas to be blank. Observations: We haven't implemented boot code that starts the loop (e.g., call reset() at end). Also there is no reset function defined; we added restartBtn but not reset. Also we haven't added input handling keys etc. So the game never starts, startLoop is never called, and `phase` is "menu", but render not called. So canvas appears blank (just background cleared, but we fill background but nothing else? Actually render gets called, but never called because startLoop not called. So canvas appears blank (maybe just background because we haven't any drawing?). So we need to add boot code that calls reset() (which we haven't defined either). Actually we need to implement reset function that sets initial state, sets phase to "playing", and calls startLoop. Or at least call startLoop directly. The simplest is add a call to startLoop(); at the end of script (boot). Also we need to define reset function that resets state and calls startLoop (so restart button works). However we have no reset function currently. The restart button is referenced via variable restartBtn but no event listener attached. Also we haven't added any logic to change phase to playing or gameover etc; but for canvas to be non-blank, at least call startLoop to draw background plus player etc. Our render draws background and player/hazards, so it would show a player circle on canvas. Phase currently = "menu". In render, we always draw background, hazards (none), player (draw player). So if startLoop runs once, it will draw player (which is a circle at (400,300) radius 10). That is visible. So we need to start loop.

Thus we need to add boot section at bottom after stub __game and after definition of restartBtn to call setup. Provide a reset function that sets phase to "playing", maybe sets initial player position and other variables, cancels loop and sets up startLoop. Since no movement yet, but it's okay. Also assign event listeners for restart button & keydown for restart.

Also include key Set for input handling (though we may not need but earlier tasks said we need it; but some parts missing now). For minimal, implement boot that sets up listeners for restart button and R-key, and calls startLoop.

We have added restartBtn variable but not used. Let's add code to set up event listeners:
- document.addEventListener('keydown', (ev)=>{ if(ev.key==='r' || ev.key==='R') reset(); })
- restartBtn.addEventListener('click', reset);
- Also define a reset function:
function reset() {
    if (loopId !== null) cancelAnimationFrame(loopId);
    // reset state
    player.x = canvas.width/2;
    player.y = canvas.height/2;
    player.r = 10; // radius maybe unchanged.
    hazards = [];
    score = 0;
    phase = 'playing';
    publishState(); // update __game and state.
    startLoop();
}
